    <h1>Divorce in New York:<br>What It Means for Your <span class="brand-italic">Finances</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">New York uses a formula for spousal maintenance and child support, but it divides property "equitably," which is not the same as equally. Before you make decisions about your home, your support, and your retirement, here is how New York actually handles the money, in plain language.</p>
    <p class="updated">Reviewed against New York divorce law as of the date noted. General financial guidance, not legal advice.</p>
