      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How is child support calculated in New York?</summary>
        <p>Under the Child Support Standards Act, the parents' combined income up to a cap is multiplied by a percentage based on the number of children: 17 percent for one, 25 percent for two, 29 percent for three, 31 percent for four, and 35 percent for five or more. Effective March 1, 2026, the income cap is $193,000. The total is then split between the parents in proportion to their incomes, plus add-ons such as childcare and medical costs.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is spousal support taxable in New York?</summary>
